/-!
# Top-degree injectivity of the cup product on `X ×_A X`

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring and `f : X ⟶ Spec A` proper and smooth of relative dimension `n`,
with `Γ(Spec A, 𝒪) ⟶ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` an isomorphism and a section `σ`. Write `W = X ×_A X` with
projections `p₁`, `p₂`, and `Ω = Ωⁿ_{X/A}`. If `Hⁿ(X, Ω)` is generated by a class `ξ` over
`A' = Γ(Spec A, 𝒪)`, then the map `x ↦ p₂^*x ∪ p₁^*ξ`,
`Hⁿ(X, Ω) ⟶ H^{2n}(W, p₂^*Ω ⊗ p₁^*Ω)`, is injective. This is the step "since we are looking in
top degree" of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0G8J].

The proof is the source's. Represent `ξ` by `t : 𝒪_X[-n] ⟶ Ω[0]`. Up to isomorphisms on both
sides, the cup product with `p₁^*ξ` is `H^{2n}` of `Lp₂^*Ω[0] ⊗^𝐋 Lp₁^*t` on
`RΓ(W, Lp₂^*Ω[0] ⊗^𝐋 Lp₁^*𝒪_X[-n])`, which is the target of a Künneth isomorphism. By
naturality of the Künneth map this becomes `1 ⊗ RΓ(X, t)` on `RΓ(X, Ω) ⊗^𝐋 RΓ(X, 𝒪_X[-n])`. The
vanishing `Stacks.WeilDeRham.retractionVanishing_single` factors `RΓ(X, t)` through a retraction
`s : RΓ(X, 𝒪_X[-n]) ⟶ A'[-n]` built from the pullback along `σ`. In the top degree,
`H^{2n}(K ⊗^𝐋 L) = Hⁿ(K) ⊗ Hⁿ(L)` for `K, L ∈ D^{≤ n}(A')` ([Stacks, Tag 068H]), so the
remaining factor `A'[-n] ⟶ RΓ(X, Ω)` acts as `y ⊗ 1 ↦ y ⊗ ξ`, which is injective because `ξ`
generates. Finally `1 ⊗ s` is detected by the pullback along the section `(σ ∘ f, id)` of `p₂`,
under which `p₂^*x` becomes `x`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.topFormsSections`: `Hⁿ(RΓ(X, Ωⁿ))` as a module over `Γ(Spec A, 𝒪)`.
* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.PullbackCupTopInjective`: the statement above.

## Main results

* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.pullbackCupTopInjective`: the statement holds.
* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.pullbackCupTopInjective_of_isIso`: the same, granted the two Künneth
  isomorphisms through `X ×_A X`.
* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.eq_zero_of_cohomologyMapOfSingleHom_eq_zero`: the derived form of the
  argument, for a morphism `(p₂^*F)[-n] ⟶ P[0]` that is `Lp₂^*F[0] ⊗^𝐋 Lp₁^*t` up to
  isomorphisms.
* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.pullbackSections_eq_zero_of_homology_map_tensor_eq_zero`: the argument on
  ringed spaces: a top-degree class killed by `1 ⊗ Lp^*t` restricts to zero along the section.
* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.injective_homology_map_tensor_top`: top-degree injectivity of `K ⊗^𝐋 v`
  over a commutative ring.
* `Stacks.WeilDeRham.cup_eq_cohomologyMapOfSingleHom_cupEdge`,
  `Stacks.WeilDeRham.isIso_cupEdgeLeft`, `Stacks.WeilDeRham.isIso_cupEdgeRight`: the cup product
  with a represented class through explicit factors, and their invertibility, the second for a
  flat factor.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.WeilDeRham.exists_cup_eq_cohomologyMapOfSingleHom` states the cup product formula with
its two outer factors existentially quantified. Here their invertibility is needed, so the
formula is restated at its witnesses `cupEdgeLeft` and `cupEdgeRight`, with the same proof.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G8J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G8J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 068H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/068H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FLQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FLQ)
-/

